  "name": "Caledon Highport",
  "description": "Caledon Highport, the first space station: a ring of sixteen habitat segments 264 m across round one hexagonal hub under a command dome, joined by three spokes. Landing pads for Shuttles and Limpets on the ring's roof, hangars in its walls; under the hub a docking spindle with the customs drum, a dock collar with Magpie berths east and west, a freight collar with Dray berths, a frigate collar with Zero Day berths north and south (one line of berths to a level), and engineering with its radiators, the reactor and the station-keeping drives at its foot.",
